'=====================================================================
' Agent name : BulkReg\11 - Batch Manager
' Version    : 4.5.0  (BulkReg release; libraries BulkRegCommon + BulkRegAgents 4.5.0)
' Code       : ALL logic is in the script library BulkRegAgents (BR_RunBatchManager).
'              This agent only calls it, so it never changes between releases.
'
' HOW TO INSTALL: open the agent, click in the editor, Ctrl+A, Delete, paste this
'              WHOLE file, Ctrl+S. Designer puts each part in its place automatically.
' Designer   : Shared agent, LotusScript
'              Runtime: On event > Action menu selection, Target: None
'              (NOT 'All selected documents' - Designer's default - or Notes asks for a selected document)
'              (backslash in the name = Actions > BulkReg submenu; do NOT use '|')
'
' What it does (details: BulkRegAgents > BR_RunBatchManager):
'
' Lists every BATCH-*.csv with its state (OPEN, STOPPED, DONE_INCOMPLETE, DONE_COMPLETE), how many rows are
' registered / not registered / gone, failures, last activity and what to do next; writes BATCHSTATUS_<run>.csv
' in BatchDir. Optional, each confirmed with YES:
'   RESUME <id>    re-open a DONE batch that still has unregistered users, then run 03
'   REMAINDER <id> write BATCH-<id>-R1.csv with only the unregistered rows (review it, then run 03)
'   CLOSE <id>     remove the flag of a STOPPED batch (treat as DONE) or close an OPEN batch
' Changes only files in BatchDir. Reads the Domino Directory, changes nothing there.
'=====================================================================
'#####################################################################
' --- part 1: (Options) ---
'#####################################################################
Option Public
Option Declare
Use "BulkRegAgents"
'#####################################################################
' --- part 2: Initialize ---
'#####################################################################
Sub Initialize
	Call BR_RunBatchManager()
End Sub
